    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/administration-and-training-coordinator-fixed-term-ps50968": {
      "title": "Administration and Training Coordinator (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Administration and Training Coordinator (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Administration and Training Coordinator (Fixed Term) Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Administration and Training Coordinator (Fixed Term) The Administration and Training Coordinator will be based in the Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (CSCI) and will support the Project/Grant Manager to deliver administration and training activities for the recently awarded UK National Hub (£25M) held in the CSCI. The UK Hub for Predictive and AI-Enabled Human Disease Models is a UK national research initiative funded by MRC, which will translate academic New Approach Methodologies (NAMs) into validated, industry-ready systems. Administration and training are core operational functions across the Hub which will join forces with existing administration and training structures to provide a comprehensive support to CSCI. The purpose of the role is to provide high quality administrative to the Hub providing support to the Senior Leadership team and the Senior Programme Manager. Delivery of these objectives will come by providing a high-quality, proactive and effective support service. The post will also support the admissions processes and course(s) support systems within the Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (CSCI) and Hub in order to provide an efficient admissions experience for prospective students, key support for current students and organise the course schedule and two annual student events. We are seeking a proactive and highly organised Administration and Training Coordinator to play a central support role in the delivery and development of our ambitious Hub programme. They will also provide essential administrative support for the Hub's apprenticeship programmes, ensuring the efficient coordination, monitoring, and delivery of apprenticeship-related processes and activities. The successful candidate will have previous administration skills or related relevant administrative support experience. An understanding of the biomedical research in the Higher Education sector would also be helpful. They will be comfortable operating in a fast-paced academic environment and able to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders, including researchers, clinicians, funders, and external commercial partners. Full-time (1.0 FTE; change to part time and flexible working arrangements available); Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available until 31 March 2030 in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference PS50968 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Cambridge Stem Cell Institute (SBS) Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference PS50968 Category Assistant staff Date published 4 September 2026 Closing date 1 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/assistant-professor-in-islamic-philosophy-gf50963": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Islamic Philosophy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Islamic Philosophy | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Assistant Professor in Islamic Philosophy Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Assistant Professor in Islamic Philosophy The Faculty of Divinity wishes to appoint to an Assistant Professorship in Islamic Philosophy from 1 September 2027. The postholder will be based in the Faculty of Divinity, West Road, Cambridge. Applicants should have a doctorate in Islamic Philosophy and either a proven track record of, or demonstrable potential for high quality research and publications in any aspect of Medieval Islamic Philosophy. The successful candidate will be required to teach on the Undergraduate Tripos, Advanced Diploma and the MPhil, as well as to supervise doctoral students and to undertake administrative duties within the Faculty. The person appointed will be expected to deliver around 40-48 lecture-room contact hours of teaching across the three terms of the academic year.  This will involve a substantial contribution to teaching in part II of the 'Tripos' (i.e. the second and third years of the BA Hons programme), including some teaching in Qur'anic Arabic, and at least one module for the MPhil. Together with colleagues in the Religious Studies section of the Faculty, the appointee will share responsibility for designing and delivering the Faculty's teaching in the field of Islamic Studies. The successful applicant will also be expected to undertake College teaching for additional remuneration. Applicants need to upload the following documents on that system: Your Curriculum Vitae (CV) with a list of publications A covering letter A statement of research plans of no more than two sides of A4 An outline of a course of 8 lectures introducing second-year undergraduates to key themes in medieval Islamic philosophy or Philosophical theology (no more than 4 sides A4) A sample of published or completed research (journal article, chapter from book or dissertation) of no more than around 8000 words The online system will ask for the names and contact details of 3 referees. References will be taken up only after shortlisting. Informal enquiries about the post may be made to Professor Richard Rex, Chair of the Faculty Board, rawr1@cam.ac.uk . For questions on the application process, please contact the School's HR team on sahhr@admin.cam.ac.uk The closing date is midnight (BST) on Friday 16 October 2026.  It is expected that interviews will be held in late January or early February 2027. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Please quote reference GF50963 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and we particularly welcome applications from candidates from a Black, Asian or Minority Ethnic background for this vacancy, as people from these backgrounds are currently underrepresented at this level in our Faculty. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Faculty of Divinity Salary £47,389-£59,966 Reference GF50963 Category Academic Date published 9 September 2026 Closing date 16 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
