    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/assistantassociate-professor-in-accounting-ns48633-0": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor in Accounting | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor in Accounting Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Assistant/Associate Professor in Accounting Cambridge Judge Business School (CJBS) invites applications for a faculty position with the Accounting Group at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Judge Business School is part of the University of Cambridge, giving faculty extensive opportunities to collaborate with researchers across the University. Cambridge also sits at the centre of \"Silicon Fen\", one of Europe's leading technology and innovation clusters, creating opportunities for research and engagement with entrepreneurs, start-ups, investors and established companies. The Accounting Group's research interests span financial and managerial accounting and related areas. Current areas include financial reporting and disclosure, auditing, corporate governance, disinformation, executive compensation and incentives, management control and performance measurement, capital markets, financial institutions, and sustainability and ESG reporting. We welcome outstanding candidates from all areas of accounting. The successful candidate will hold, or be close to completing, a PhD in Accounting or a related discipline. They will be expected to produce internationally excellent research published in leading international journals, contribute to teaching and supervision across the School's programmes, and take an active part in the intellectual life of the Accounting Group. We value research that is both rigorous and consequential - work that advances the academic literature while also speaking to the questions facing standard setters, regulators, firms and investors. The School actively supports faculty in bringing their research to bear on policy and practice, and in bringing that engagement back into their teaching. Evidence of intellectual excellence is the primary criterion for appointment. Depending on career stage, this may take the form of publications in leading journals, high-quality working papers at an advanced stage of the review process, and a strong pipeline of ongoing research. For appointment at the Associate Professor level, candidates are expected to have an established record of internationally excellent publications together with a continuing pipeline of high-quality work. The start date is negotiable: the appointment can begin at any point between January and September 2027, to be agreed with the successful candidate. The School offers a competitive salary and benefits package. Applications should include:\n-   Curriculum vitae.\n-   Cover letter explaining your interest in the post.\n-   A sample of research that best represents your work, such as a job market paper together with other working papers or publications.\n-   A one-page statement of research interests and future plans.\n-   Evidence of teaching performance, if available.\n-   The names and contact details of three professional referees. We do not contact referees at the point of application. Candidates who currently hold an academic post may ask us to defer approaching their referees until the later stages of the process, and we will confirm with them before making contact. Shortlisted applicants will be invited to Cambridge for a visit to the School, informal discussions with faculty, a research presentation and a formal interview. Interviews are expected to take place in late October 2026. We encourage early applications. The closing date for applications is 4 October 2026. We may extend this date if necessary, and will continue to consider applications until the position is filled. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our department/institution/Faculty/School/University. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries about the post are welcome and should be directed to Professor Rafael Rogo at r.rogo@jbs.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference NS48633 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Judge Business School Salary £63,606-£67,468 Reference NS48633 Category Academic Date published 8 September 2026 Closing date 4 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/clinical-lecturer-health-and-social-care-regulated-professional-post-in-nhs-england-ra50937": {
      "title": "Clinical Lecturer (Health and Social Care Regulated Professional) Post in NHS England",
      "description": "Clinical Lecturer (Health and Social Care Regulated Professional) Post in NHS England | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Clinical Lecturer (Health and Social Care Regulated Professional) Post in NHS England Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Clinical Lecturer (Health and Social Care Regulated Professional) Post in NHS England Applications are invited for a Clinical Lecturer post for a Health and Social Care Regulated Professional. This role is available to nurses, midwives, allied health professionals (NMAHPs) and pharmacists. The post is for a maximum of four years. The aim of this post is to provide time and support for an early post-doctoral NMAHP to develop their clinical academic career, conduct preliminary research, and receive support and training to enable them to be successful in securing a post-doctoral or intermediate-level research fellowship. This Clinical Lecturer post is 50% clinical and 50% research, with the time to be taken flexibly. The post is not limited by clinical specialty, area of health and/or care services, or research focus, provided the proposed work will benefit patients and/or public health. The successful post-holder will continue in their clinical role within their employing organisation at 50% full-time equivalent (FTE) and therefore retain their employment rights and pension. The 50% FTE research time will be funded by NHSE East of England in collaboration with the University of Cambridge, where the post-holder will hold a secondment contract/visiting researcher agreement in an appropriate department. The choice of academic department should be determined by the applicant's field of research and should provide the most suitable research-active environment and mentorship to support their career goals. Funding will be allocated directly to the NHS host organisation by NHSE East of England. Salary Commensurate with current salary. Eligibility Applicants must meet all of the following criteria: Hold a registration with either the HCPC or the NMC. Be employed by a provider of health and/or care services that delivers at least 50% of its services free at the point of delivery. Spend approximately 50% of their current role delivering health and/or care services that are free at the point of delivery. Work in the East of England NHS region. Have completed their PhD or have submitted their thesis and completed their viva with only minor corrections required at the time of interview, with confirmation of a pass from the HEI by the date of commencement in post. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Applications Please submit 1) A full CV and covering letter and 2) a supporting statement (maximum three A4 pages) addressing: Your research experience to date Your plans for developing your programme of research, including research collaborations and potential fellowship or grant applications How this post will advance your development as a clinical academic and independent investigator Additionally, please provide: A letter of support from your proposed mentor or research team leader within your chosen department at the University of Cambridge. The names of three referees (please indicate whether they may be contacted prior to interview). A letter from your NHS line manager confirming that, if successful at interview, you will be released from your clinical commitments to undertake this role The closing date for applications is 30 September 2026, with interviews anticipated to take place on 30 October 2026. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to Professor Joanne McPeake at jm2565@cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference RA50937 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Office of the School of Clinical Medicine Salary Commensurate with current salary Reference RA50937 Category Academic Date published 3 September 2026 Closing date 30 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/dairy-herdsperson-fixed-term-xm50989": {
      "title": "Dairy Herdsperson (Fixed Term)",
      "description": "Dairy Herdsperson (Fixed Term) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Dairy Herdsperson (Fixed Term) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Dairy Herdsperson (Fixed Term) The University of Cambridge is seeking an experienced and dedicated Dairy Herdsperson to join the team at the Cambridge University Farm (CUF). CUF operates as a commercial farm while providing an exemplar teaching facility for the Vet School, supporting clinical teaching and maintaining high welfare and compliance standards. The livestock enterprise includes a high yielding dairy herd of approximately 220 milking cows producing around 2 million litres of milk per year, alongside a 250 head sheep flock. About the role As a key member of the dairy team, you will contribute to the safe, efficient and compliant operation of the dairy herd. Working closely with the Dairy Farm Manager, you will support long term herd planning, daily herd management, robotic milking operations, breeding and youngstock care. The role also supports the teaching needs of the Vet School, ensuring animals are available for clinical teaching as required. This is a hands on role requiring strong practical skills, sound judgement and the ability to work independently. You will participate in an alternate weekend rota and a one in four on call rota for robotic milking systems and night checks. Key responsibilities Dairy herd management, including planning breeding programmes, monitoring milk production and ensuring accurate record keeping. Oversight of robotic milking systems, including preventative and corrective maintenance and ensuring cows are milked at appropriate frequencies. Monitoring animal health and welfare, identifying issues such as mastitis, lameness and metabolic conditions, and liaising with Vets as required. Artificial insemination, including identifying bulling, handling straws correctly and maintaining breeding records. Calving and calf rearing, recognising signs of calving, assisting safely, managing colostrum, rearing calves and carrying out disbudding and castration. Feeding operations, including feeding 240 dairy cows and 200 youngstock, adjusting feed mixes and operating feeding equipment. Dry cow management, including dietary monitoring and drying off cows in line with herd policy. Ensuring compliance with assurance schemes and regulatory bodies such as DEFRA, the RPA and the Environment Agency, and maintaining a safe working environment for staff, students and visitors. About you Extensive practical experience in modern dairy herd management, ideally within a high yielding herd environment. Strong knowledge of modern farming methods and agricultural machinery. Understanding of regulatory bodies such as DEFRA, the RPA and the Environment Agency. Good communication skills, particularly when working with Vets and students. Ability to work effectively with minimal supervision. Good IT skills and accurate record keeping capability. S/NVQ Level 3 in Livestock Production (Dairy) or equivalent experience. A full, clean UK driving licence. Please be aware that a Full UK Driving Licence is essential for this role (a full EU Driving Licence is acceptable on appointment, but the successful applicant must transfer to a UK Licence prior to confirming a start date). Commitment to ongoing professional development and keeping up to date with industry developments. We offer: Accommodation is provided on site due to the requirements of the role. Relocation Package is available. Standby Payment Allowance for being part of the standby rota including weekends for our robotic milking system alarms. Fixed-term: The funds for this post are available for 2 years in the first instance. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please email Estates Division on EDR@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference XM50989 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Dairy Herdsperson Key information Department/location Estates Division (Business Services) Salary £27,319-£31,236 Reference XM50989 Category Assistant staff Date published 11 September 2026 Closing date 22 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/deputy-biofacility-manager-aq51033": {
      "title": "Deputy Biofacility Manager",
      "description": "Deputy Biofacility Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Deputy Biofacility Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Deputy Biofacility Manager We are looking to recruit an experienced and motivated Deputy Biofacility Manager to be part of a hardworking team in a busy biomedical facility situated in Cambridge.\nYou will assist the Biofacility manager with the day to day management of the biofacility and deputise in their absence. You will coordinate the animal husbandry work of the facility, supervising a team of technicians, coordinating the activity and staffing allocations of the team to ensure the smooth day-to-day running of the facility and maintain high standards of animal care and welfare. You will assist the Biofacility Manager with the recruitment, training and assessment of new staff with in-house policies and procedures as well as working to Home Office regulations and performance management. You will undertake both licenced and unlicensed scientific procedures along with daily husbandry and maintenance to assist the technicians as required. You are responsible for the maintenance of all necessary records, referring any issues and concerns to the Biofacility Manager as necessary. You will be able to work both independently and as part of a team, with experience supervising or managing staff. You will have IAT Level 3 or equivalent, Home Office Licence modules A - C and will be a Personal Licence holder. In depth experience of working within a biofacility with conventional and IVCs is essential, as are excellent communication skills. You must be able to use a computerised data management system and have previous experience working in a supervisory / team leader role. Knowledge of relevant Home Office, and Health and Safety legislation is important, as is knowledge and experience in the principals of aseptic surgery and specialised breeding techniques. The facility operates a rota system to provide animal care and essential husbandry at weekends and over Bank Holidays. The role holder will be required to participate on an out of hours call out list also. In addition to the base salary stated above, the successful candidate for this post will receive an additional 2.5% supplement to their pay. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a health assessment and a security check. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Informal enquiries are welcomed and should be directed to UBSRecruitment@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference AQ51033 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference AQ51033 Category Assistant staff Date published 11 September 2026 Closing date 9 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/emba-programmes-coordinator-ns49767-0": {
      "title": "EMBA Programmes Coordinator",
      "description": "EMBA Programmes Coordinator | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs EMBA Programmes Coordinator Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs EMBA Programmes Coordinator We are seeking a highly organised and proactive Programme Coordinator to join the Executive MBA (EMBA) Office. This is a varied and fast-paced role, offering the opportunity to contribute to the delivery of a globally recognised Executive MBA experience. You will play a key part in ensuring the smooth running of programme activities and events, helping to maintain the exceptional standards of service and professionalism associated with CJBS, while working closely with a diverse and international community of students, faculty, and partners. About the role: The EMBA office runs the operations, course delivery, events, faculty support and student services for the Executive MBA programmes. This role will play a crucial part in course administration and event management of both small- and large-scale events, including the EMBA College dinners, Orientation Week, International Business Study Trips, Electives Week, the Cambridge Ecosystem week and Graduation. The role holder will therefore interact with a diverse customer base of professional students, faculty, and staff, as well as university and external event services. As such, the EMBA Programmes Coordinator plays a central role in the high level of customer service necessary to maintain the excellent reputation of CJBS. The ideal candidate should have the following qualities, skills and attributes: Previous course administration experience or a high level of administration experience working with senior executives Event experience ideally at an executive level with both small and large-scale events. Demonstrable customer service experience working with executive clients or similar clientele. Excellent organisational skills with a clear, strong, demonstrable level of attention to detail and strong time management/prioritisation skills Excellent written and spoken communication & interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to work under pressure. Ability to demonstrate the confidence and awareness to manage and support student welfare matters and highly sensitive casework in an appropriate and professional manner. Educated to at least A level or with equivalent relevant experience. Strong IT skills: excellent all-round ability in using Microsoft Office suite (higher level skills in Word, Excel and PowerPoint preferred). Skills and knowledge of eLearning technology;   skilled at quickly learning and adapting to new technologies and has a strong interest in  promoting and proposing ways of improving processes and systems Why work for Cambridge Judge Business School? We are the business school of the University of Cambridge, advancing knowledge and leadership through people who leave a mark on the world. Cambridge Judge Business School leverages the power of academia for real world impact to transform individuals, organisations and society. Since 1990, we have forged a reputation as a centre of rigorous thinking and high-impact transformative education, situated within one of the world's most prestigious research universities, and in the heart of the Cambridge Cluster, the most successful technology entrepreneurship cluster in Europe. Benefits of working for Cambridge Judge Business School: You'll receive excellent benefits at Cambridge Judge Business School including: Generous holiday allowance Defined benefits pension schemes Flexible working options Family-friendly initiatives Career development opportunities Support for health and mental wellbeing Discounts on shopping Tax-efficient bicycle and charity-giving schemes More information is available on our website -Staff benefits - Jobs at Cambridge Judge Business School - Cambridge Judge Business School Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Application process: To view more details about the role and person specification, please click the Further Information link. Closing Date: 27 September 2026 Interview Dates: w/c 5 October 2026 If you have any queries regarding the application process, please contact: hrsupport@jbs.cam.ac.uk Additional Information: The University is supportive of hybrid working, where some work is undertaken on University premises and some in a remote working environment. The aim of our approach is to enable as many staff as possible to work in a hybrid way if they wish and where their role allows we expect most colleagues to spend at least 50% of their time at their dedicated office location. This arrangement is subject to change and will not form a part of the contractual terms of the role. Please ensure that you outline how you match the criteria for the post and why you are applying for this role on the online application form. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which must be your most recent line manager. Please quote reference NS49767 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Judge Business School Salary £31,236-£35,608 Reference NS49767 Category Assistant staff Date published 14 September 2026 Closing date 27 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/endpoint-specialist-vc50971": {
      "title": "Endpoint Specialist",
      "description": "Endpoint Specialist | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Skip to main content Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Research at Cambridge For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Endpoint Specialist Jobs Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Endpoint Specialist University Information Services (UIS) provides the digital infrastructure, business information and computing services at the heart of one of the world's top universities. The University of Cambridge has a bold ambition to use digitalisation to transform education and research, and UIS' team of developers, designers, testers, analysts and support staff is leading this exciting work. The role The Endpoint Specialist will join a team providing managed Windows & macOS devices as part of the University Managed Desktop to enable staff and students to work in a secure and productive manner in alignment with the University's digital aims.\nYou'll get the chance to collaborate and interact with some of the finest minds in the world, sharing data, insight and expertise to make a meaningful difference to the University's success while using best practice tooling and methodologies. What you will do As a Endpoint Specialist you will: Contribute to the University Managed Desktop service, packaging applications, deploying configurations and developing new features. Implement and maintain automated services at scale. Develop and document procedures for supporting teams. Work with UMD customers within the University to ensure the University Managed Desktop aligns with a wide range of requirements. Provide platform specific technical advice to support other UIS services. What you will need Experience of managing Windows devices at scale, preferably using Microsoft cloud technologies. Good communication, organisational and problem-solving skills deploying. Proven ability to work in a diverse environment with complex requirements. Ability to use PowerShell scripting for task automation and system management is desirable. Experience of integrating scripts with APIs, with Microsoft Graph API being highly advantageous. The benefits You can expect to receive: A competitive salary with service-related progression and annual cost-of-living increases. A generous annual leave allowance of 41 days (including bank holidays). A generous pension scheme with attractive employer contributions. Access to a range of shopping and travel discounts through the CAMbens scheme. This position is a permanent, full-time role, currently based on the University's West Cambridge Site. University Information Services will be moving to new accommodation on Brooklands Avenue in March 2027. The nature of this post requires attendance at the office of a minimum of one day a week, sometimes more depending on work requirements. Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you would like more information about this role, informal enquiries can be directed by email to recruitment@uis.cam.ac.uk . Please quote reference VC50971 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Information Services Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference VC50971 Category Academic-related Date published 4 September 2026 Closing date 25 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
