      "title": "Research Support Librarian (SBS)",
      "description": "Research Support Librarian (SBS) | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Research Support Librarian (SBS) Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Research Support Librarian (SBS) Ever wanted to work in an institution that is home to one of the world's great collections of cultural treasures and research materials? Spanning thousands of years of human thought and discovery, Cambridge University Libraries and Archives house unique treasures and research materials made up of nearly ten million books, maps, manuscripts, photographs and priceless objects. We are seeking a collaborative and proactive Research Support Librarian to join the Biological Sciences Libraries Team. This is an exciting opportunity to play a leading role in delivering specialist research support services across the School of Biological Sciences (SBS), helping researchers maximise the quality, visibility, and impact of their work. The role The Research Support Librarian will provide expert guidance and training across the research lifecycle, supporting open research, systematic reviews and research assessment across the School of Biological Sciences (SBS). Working closely with researchers and colleagues across Cambridge University Libraries and Archives, you will help advance research excellence and contribute to the delivery of high-quality library services across the Downing and West Cambridge sites. As a Research Support Librarian (SBS) you will Develop and deliver research support services tailored to the needs of the School of Biological Sciences, representing and advocating for its research priorities. Engage in data-driven evaluation of services and resources to ensure their suitability, identify new needs and support continuous improvement. Lead the delivery of targeted research skills training for the SBS research community. Drive the development of the Biological Sciences Libraries' digital presence through engaging, user-focused web pages and SharePoint content. Contribute to shared team goals by collaborating effectively and fostering a supportive team culture. What we are looking for Knowledge of open research, scholarly communication and research data management. Proven ability to develop strong relationships and partnerships with stakeholders. Experience delivering teaching, training, or learning support both online and in-person. Knowledge of academic information resources and databases, with experience in developing user-focused STEM library collections and services. A customer-focused professional with a commitment to excellent service and flexibility to work across multiple sites. What we offer Flexible working arrangements are available upon discussion. Hybrid working and flexible hours are limited due to the operational requirements of the role. If needed, please contact us to discuss. Generous annual leave allowance of 36 days. Exceptional parental leave (including maternity, paternity / co-parent, adoption and shared parental leave). Discounts on major retailers. Professional development opportunities such as apprenticeships and access to a variety of training courses. We welcome applications from individuals who wish to be considered for part-time working or other flexible working arrangements. We particularly welcome applications from women and /or candidates from a BME background for this vacancy as they are currently under-represented at this level in our School. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you wish to discuss any aspects of the role please contact : - Funmike Ifie, Biological Sciences Librarian. Tel: 0776 1044287  - Email: yoi20@cam.ac.uk Application closing date: Sunday 20 September 2026. Interview date: Thursday 15 October 2026. For further details please refer to the Further Particulars. Please quote reference VE50905 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Particulars Key information Department/location University Library Salary £33,951-£39,906 Reference VE50905 Category Assistant staff Date published 3 September 2026 Closing date 20 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/rokos-school-of-government-business-and-operations-manager-lr51022": {
      "title": "Rokos School of Government Business and Operations Manager",
      "description": "Rokos School of Government Business and Operations Manager | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Rokos School of Government Business and Operations Manager Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Rokos School of Government Business and Operations Manager The Rokos School of Government (RSG) is being established to prepare a new generation of leaders capable of addressing the world's most complex challenges.  Initially to act as the Dean's principal partner in establishing and rapidly scaling up the new RSG, the Business Operations Manager will lead the development of the RSG's core structures and systems and ensure effective operational delivery. The post holder will design, recruit and lead the RSG's Professional Services team, they will advise and support the Dean in developing strategic priorities, and in building key external relationships.  Over the first five years, they will help drive an ambitious growth plan - expanding education and research programmes, partnerships, staffing, and resources - to position the RSG as a nationally and internationally recognised centre of excellence. Adept in networking appropriately, the post holder will develop and maintain constructive dialogue and communication with key contacts across the School, the wider University and externally in order to influence developments and promote and enhance RSG activities.  The post holder will have extensive experience in senior administrative roles and operational management, a record of leadership and experience of managing and developing professional teams, significant experience of strategic financial planning and budget management and be able to deliver in a complex and devolved environment. Candidates must have a degree level education or equivalent. You will have excellent organisational skills, the ability to work on your own initiative, prioritise work, work to tight deadlines and have excellent people management and communication skills. For an informal discussion about the post, please contact Dr Jim Bellingham, SecSPS@admin.cam.ac.uk . Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. Further details on the position can be found in the Further Particulars document. Please ensure that you upload your Curriculum Vitae (CV), a covering letter and publications list in the upload section. If you upload any additional documents that have not been requested they will not be considered as part of your application. Please include details of your referees, including email address and phone number, one of which should be your most recent line manager. The interview date for the role is to be confirmed, likely week commencing Monday 26th October 2026. Please quote reference LR51022 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Rokos School of Government Salary £63,606-£67,468 Reference LR51022 Category Academic-related Date published 10 September 2026 Closing date 11 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
