    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/grounds-operative-ba50315": {
      "title": "Grounds Operative",
      "description": "Grounds Operative | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Grounds Operative Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Grounds Operative An exciting opportunity has arisen for Grounds Operative to join the Estates Division. About the Role: The role holder will assist the Grounds Maintenance team with keeping the grounds and gardens of the University estate in a safe and presentable state. University has a Biodiversity Action Plan (BAP) for the estate, which includes managing with biodiversity in mind and engaging staff, students and visitors with the changes. The role holder will help to implement this across the estate. The Grounds Maintenance team have started a renewal, refresh and refurb of the grounds and gardens of the estate and the role holder will with this on the sites they will be specifically looking after. Key Responsibilities: The role holder may occasionally be responsible for managing a team of up to 3 staff, if the supervisor is away due to illness or holiday. The role holder will support the planning and activities of the Grounds Maintenance team daily. The role holder will have some input in developing environmental, sustainability and biodiversity policies and for the management of all areas of grounds and garden across the University's estate. The role holder may assist with the induction and training of new Grounds staff and temporary staff. The role holder will assist in preparing the teams needs for the forthcoming seasons, including plants and materials required.  They will help to maintain any records such as chemical usage. The role holder may on occasions liaise with departments and other external contractors such as tree works, ground prep, grounds maintenance contractors. The role holder working with their team/teams on nominated sites and areas, to a high standard. The role holder will ensure the safe storage of and maintenance of equipment and tools including the building and/or vehicle they operate from.  And the sites they assigned to maintain. The role holder will assist in ensuring Health & Safety regulations and relevant codes of practice are implemented and observed in the day-to-day work of the section.  Undertake risk assessments associated with the Team's work as and when issues or changes in situation arise, reporting any hazards or sudden incidents. The role is site or mobile based and not hybrid.  Monday to Thursday 7 am to 3 pm, Friday 7 am to 2.30 pm.  Breaks are 10am to 10.30 am and 1 pm to 1.30 pm.  There may be occasional weekend work and out of hours working with prior arrangement. About you: For this role you will need strong interpersonal skills, which will help you with your ability to work within a team. You are able to demonstrate experience, knowledge and understanding of tools and equipment, of biodiversity and environmental techniques. It would be an advantage if you have some plant knowledge and the relevant skills and knowledge across a wide scope of tasks related to grounds maintenance.  Knowledge of using Microsoft office, PDAs and Computer-Aided Facility Management systems (Invida) Qualifications: Educated to at least GCSE standard or equivalent. Additional requirements will include: A full driving licence, including towing capability (a full EU Driving Licence is acceptable on appointment, but the successful applicant must transfer to a UK Licence prior to confirming a start date). Certification of training of various handheld machines and ride-on machines used in the grounds maintenance sector is desirable but not essential. The ability to work in a wide range of environments, and highly changeable conditions working outdoors in all weathers, adapting and adjusting working practices to ensure safety of self and others. The ability to maintain long periods of physically strenuous activity when the task requires it. To have highly detailed and developed skills to undertake precise physical movements involving fine degrees of control. Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please email Estates Division on EDR@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference BA50315 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Grounds Operative Key information Department/location Estates Division (Facilities) Salary £25,249-£27,319 Reference BA50315 Category Assistant staff Date published 15 September 2026 Closing date 29 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/head-chef-xm49872": {
      "title": "Head Chef",
      "description": "Head Chef | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Head Chef Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Head Chef About Us The University of Cambridge is one of the world's leading academic institutions, with nearly 800 years of excellence in education, research, and innovation. We are seeking a Head Chef to join us full-time (36.5 hours, Monday to Friday). Benefits Competitive salary with annual increases and progression Generous annual leave Family-friendly policies, including maternity and shared parental leave Pension scheme with strong employer contribution Staff Counselling Service Travel benefits and retail discounts Relocation support This is an excellent opportunity for an experienced chef from a large-scale catering background to lead a high-profile operation within a prestigious institution. The Role As Head Chef, you will lead high-quality food production across cafés, hospitality events, and dining services within the West Hub. You will ensure exceptional standards, compliance with food safety regulations, and effective day-to-day operations. Key responsibilities: Lead, motivate, and develop a team of chefs Plan and deliver innovative, high-quality menus Manage purchasing, stock control, and supplier relationships Ensure compliance with HACCP, hygiene, and safety standards Monitor budgets, costs, and waste Oversee staffing rotas, training, and performance management Support sustainability initiatives aligned with University policy About You You will bring: Significant experience in a similar or large-scale catering operation Strong expertise in menu planning, purchasing, and kitchen management Proven staff management and training experience Excellent customer service and communication skills In-depth knowledge of HACCP and food safety systems Relevant culinary qualification (NVQ Level 4 or equivalent) Advanced Food Hygiene Certificate (Level 4) Full driving licence Please be aware that a Full UK Driving Licence is essential for this role (a full EU Driving Licence is acceptable on appointment, but the successful applicant must transfer to a UK Licence prior to confirming a start date). You will be organised, adaptable, and passionate about delivering outstanding food and service while leading a high-performing team. Additional Information The University of Cambridge is committed to equality, diversity, and inclusion, creating a supportive environment where everyone can thrive. Apply today to take the next step in your culinary leadership Click the 'Apply' button below to register an account with our recruitment system (if you have not already) and apply online. If you have any questions about this vacancy or the application process, please email Estates Division on EDR@admin.cam.ac.uk Please quote reference XM49872 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Apply online Download further information Further Information - Head Chef Key information Department/location Estates Division (Business Services) Salary £35,608-£46,049 Reference XM49872 Category Assistant staff Date published 14 September 2026 Closing date 22 September 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
    "https://www.cam.ac.uk/jobs/head-of-hr-school-of-clinical-medicine-ah51071": {
      "title": "Head of HR",
      "description": "Head of HR - School of Clinical Medicine | University of Cambridge Sorry, you need to enable JavaScript to visit this website. Your cookie choices We use necessary cookies to make our site work. If you choose to accept optional cookies, it will help us understand your needs better and personalise what you see. Accept all cookies Decline optional cookies Choose your cookie mix Skip to main content View menu Study at Cambridge About the University Research at Cambridge Quick links For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our\n              researchers Business and\n              enterprise Colleges and\n              Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Search Search site Home Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Undergraduate courses Applying Events and open days Fees and finance Postgraduate Postgraduate courses How to apply Postgraduate events Fees and funding International\n                students Continuing education Lifelong learning Courses in education Close About the University How the\n                University and Colleges work Term dates and calendars History Map Visiting the University News Annual reports A global university Equality and diversity Events Public engagement Jobs Give to Cambridge Close Research at Cambridge Close For Cambridge students For staff For alumni For our researchers Business and enterprise Colleges and Departments Give to Cambridge Libraries Museums and collections Breadcrumb Home Jobs Head of HR - School of Clinical Medicine Jobs Menu Section - Jobs Jobs home Why Cambridge? Back to section home Why Cambridge? Why Cambridge? overview Pay and reward and employee benefits How to apply Back to section home How to apply How to apply overview Finding a role and applying online Inclusive recruitment Application tips Manage my applications Contact us Browse our vacancies Back to section home Browse our vacancies Browse our vacancies overview Academic vacancies Back to section home Academic vacancies Working as an academic at Cambridge Professional services vacancies Back to section home Professional services vacancies Working in professional services roles in Cambridge Professorships and Directorships vacancies Research vacancies Back to section home Research vacancies Working as a researcher at Cambridge Studentships Temporary employment service Search all University jobs College and affiliated institution jobs Life in Cambridge Back to section home Life in Cambridge Life in Cambridge overview Community and surroundings Getting around Relocating to Cambridge Back to section home Relocating to Cambridge Relocating to Cambridge overview Visas and immigration Right to work in the UK Accommodation and relocation support Search all University jobs Head of HR - School of Clinical Medicine Contract: Permanent Salary: £69,488 - £80,525 per annum Location: Cambridge Biomedical Campus, with hybrid working Working Pattern: Full Time Are you an experienced HR leader looking to shape the people strategy of one of the world's leading centres for clinical research, education and healthcare partnership? We're seeking an exceptional Head of HR to lead the people agenda for the School of Clinical Medicine. As the most senior HR professional supporting the School, you will provide both strategic and operational leadership across a large, complex and continually evolving environment, working closely with senior academic leaders, professional services colleagues, NHS partners and research organisations. About the role Reporting to the Assistant Director of HR, you'll be responsible for developing and delivering the School's people strategy, ensuring it supports the ambitions of the School, the wider University and key external partners. This is a highly influential leadership role where you'll work with senior stakeholders to identify workforce risks, opportunities and emerging trends, translating these into practical and innovative HR solutions. You'll lead significant organisational change programmes, oversee the delivery of a full range of HR services, and help foster a positive, inclusive culture where people can thrive. A unique aspect of the role is responsibility for the University's medical workforce service, supporting clinical staff across the University and working closely with NHS partners. Success will require balancing the strategic priorities of the School, University and NHS while delivering excellent people outcomes. What you'll be doing Leading the development and implementation of the School's people strategy. Driving organisational change, transformation and workforce planning initiatives. Ensuring high-quality delivery across HR business partnering, employee relations, resourcing and HR operations. Advising on complex, sensitive and high-risk people matters. Developing innovative HR policies and practices that support organisational objectives. Leading major HR and organisational development projects. Building strong relationships with senior leaders, NHS partners, trade unions and external stakeholders. Providing leadership and direction to the School's HR teams and fostering a collaborative, high-performing culture. We're looking for someone who has Significant senior HR leadership experience within a large and complex organisation. A strong track record of leading organisational change and implementing people strategies. Experience contributing to organisation-wide strategy, planning and transformation programmes. The ability to analyse complex issues at both strategic and operational levels and develop creative, practical solutions. Excellent communication, influencing and negotiation skills. Experience building trusted relationships with senior stakeholders across organisational boundaries. Strong people leadership skills, with an energising, collaborative and inclusive approach. Chartered CIPD membership or equivalent senior-level experience. Why join us? This is a rare opportunity to lead the HR function within one of the UK's most prestigious and influential biomedical institutions. Alongside working in a collaborative and intellectually stimulating environment, the University of Cambridge offers: The opportunity to influence strategic decisions at the highest level. Excellent professional development and leadership opportunities. Generous pension provision and 41 days annual leave including public holidays. Hybrid and flexible working arrangements. A comprehensive range of health, wellbeing and family-friendly benefits. Closing date: Thursday 8 October 2026 Once an offer of employment has been accepted, the successful candidate will be required to undergo a basic disclosure (criminal records check) check and a security check. For this role, applications will be managed by Spirehouse Recruitment. To apply, please send your CV to cambridge@spirehouse.co.uk . For further information, please contact Abbie Carr at abbie@spirehouse.co.uk . Please quote reference AH51071 on your application and in any correspondence about this vacancy. The University actively supports equality, diversity and inclusion and encourages applications from all sections of society. The University has a responsibility to ensure that all employees are eligible to live and work in the UK. Download further information Further Information Key information Department/location Human Resources Division Salary £69,488 Reference AH51071 Category Academic-related Date published 14 September 2026 Closing date 8 October 2026 Connect with us Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X YouTube © 2026 University of Cambridge Contact the University Accessibility Freedom of information Privacy policy and cookies Statement on Modern Slavery Terms and conditions University A-Z Study at Cambridge Undergraduate Postgraduate Lifelong learning Courses in education About the University How the University\n              and Colleges work Give to Cambridge Jobs Map Visiting the University Cambridge University Press & Assessment Research at Cambridge Research news About research at Cambridge Public engagement"
    },
